WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:07.799
[moody, intense intro music plays]

01:09.235 --> 01:12.655
SUMMER OF 2012

01:13.990 --> 01:15.075
KOO SEONG-HEE

01:17.619 --> 01:19.079
SON MYEONG-O

01:21.456 --> 01:22.791
MORE TATTOOS? I'M SO COOL

01:22.874 --> 01:24.292
LEE SA-RA

01:24.375 --> 01:25.794
FINISHED MY PAINTING. CHEERS!

01:25.877 --> 01:27.295
WHAT TO WEAR? SO MANY CLOTHES

01:41.184 --> 01:42.352
You spying?

01:43.978 --> 01:45.355
Those IVs help you paint?

01:45.438 --> 01:47.982
What's in them
makes you a little more obedient.

01:52.112 --> 01:53.113
Five hundred grams.

01:53.613 --> 01:54.614
Careful with it.

01:54.697 --> 01:58.451
[sighs] Well, God,
we thank thee for this daily bread.

02:00.578 --> 02:03.331
Five hundred grams. Bullshit, you asshole.

02:03.414 --> 02:05.625
Don't stiff me
on my source of inspiration.

02:05.708 --> 02:07.669
You're not an artist, you're a stoner.

02:08.628 --> 02:11.798
Gonna use that thing in your hair
to draw the Mona Lisa?

02:11.881 --> 02:14.134
The Mona Lisa's
the only art you know, right?

02:14.217 --> 02:15.510
Of course it is, dumbass.

02:16.719 --> 02:20.849
[sighs] I'll let this one slide
because you're just such a little puppy.

02:20.932 --> 02:23.143
[whines, imitates puppy yapping]

02:26.187 --> 02:27.188
[scoffs]

02:27.272 --> 02:28.273
[door closes]

02:28.857 --> 02:31.109
Ah, Jesus, she's such a fucking bitch.

02:31.609 --> 02:33.444
CHOI HYE-JEONG

02:39.450 --> 02:40.660
JEON JAE-JUN

02:40.743 --> 02:42.203
FIVE DAYS AGO

02:42.287 --> 02:43.580
SIESTA

02:53.590 --> 02:55.175
Do you need anything, sir?

02:58.261 --> 02:59.929
Why don't you sing me a lullaby?

03:00.013 --> 03:01.347
I can't sleep.

03:01.431 --> 03:03.892
Would you like me
to get you a warm wet towel set?

03:03.975 --> 03:06.269
I'd like something else
that's warm and wet.

03:12.483 --> 03:14.235
Calm down and sleep tight.

03:14.319 --> 03:16.613
-[PA system beeps]
-[attendant over PA] Dear passengers,

03:16.696 --> 03:21.034
to ensure a safe flight, use of any
electronic devices is not allowed.

03:21.117 --> 03:23.369
[phone keyboard clicking]

03:23.453 --> 03:26.456
[Hye-jeong] I'm so tired.
Can you give me a ride?

03:26.539 --> 03:28.374
NEW MESSAGE
JAE-JUN

03:28.458 --> 03:29.459
[faucet running]

03:36.883 --> 03:37.884
[phone chimes]

03:42.847 --> 03:45.391
[Jae-jun] Drink a Bacchus
and take the airport bus. I'm busy.

03:49.062 --> 03:50.563
Hey, can I try this one on?

03:51.940 --> 03:52.857
I'm so sorry.

03:54.025 --> 03:56.611
We have some water leakage
in the fitting rooms.

03:56.694 --> 03:58.780
But I can give you 10% off instead.

03:59.364 --> 04:02.867
You don't need to try this on,
it looks like it was made for you.

04:03.576 --> 04:08.498
UNDER MAINTENANCE
SORRY FOR THE INCONVENIENCE

04:08.581 --> 04:09.582
[both panting]

04:26.683 --> 04:27.684
[moans]

04:31.688 --> 04:33.690
[breathing evens out]

04:39.612 --> 04:43.825
Did I ever tell you
why this store is called the Siesta?

04:47.078 --> 04:49.706
Because you like
sleeping with me during the day?

04:53.793 --> 04:54.794
Yeah. You're right.

04:56.629 --> 04:58.715
So you can see some other bitch at night?

05:00.049 --> 05:01.050
[breathy gasp]

05:02.677 --> 05:03.678
[Jae-jun clears throat]

05:05.179 --> 05:06.180
[Yeon-jin groans]

05:08.641 --> 05:10.226
How are wedding preparations?

05:10.768 --> 05:12.895
Why do you ask when you don't really care?

05:13.688 --> 05:15.231
Makes me seem nice.

05:15.315 --> 05:16.733
[chuckles] Bullshit.

05:19.527 --> 05:21.696
Let me know
if you ever want to get married.

05:22.613 --> 05:24.991
Because I don't like to share
with other women.

05:26.993 --> 05:28.995
[subdued, mysterious music playing]

05:29.495 --> 05:30.580
[glasses clink]

05:31.080 --> 05:32.623
PARK YEON-JIN

05:34.250 --> 05:35.501
WAITING FOR MY BABE

05:35.585 --> 05:36.753
AMAZING VIEW, THANK YOU

05:36.836 --> 05:38.463
WHICH DRESS? THEY'RE ALL SO PRETTY

05:47.388 --> 05:49.265
A LOT TO PREPARE, BUT I'M HAPPY! LOVE YOU!

06:18.169 --> 06:20.213
[Seong-hee typing]

06:21.255 --> 06:23.591
-Having fun at work?
-Yeah, lots of fun.

06:24.384 --> 06:26.636
The manager really likes you, you know.

06:26.719 --> 06:30.556
Apparently, since you started
tutoring their daughter,

06:31.057 --> 06:33.267
she started wearing less makeup.

06:36.854 --> 06:37.980
[Seong-hee] Got it.

06:38.981 --> 06:42.318
You know, I think she's starting
to move over to Instagram.

06:42.402 --> 06:44.487
That bitch Hye-jeong already switched.

06:46.114 --> 06:48.199
She doesn't do Facebook anymore?

06:48.991 --> 06:50.576
Cheer up, okay?

06:50.660 --> 06:52.703
Did you think revenge would be easy?

06:53.246 --> 06:55.665
When they all make the switch,
just use this account.

06:55.748 --> 06:58.251
The ID and password are
the same as the Facebook account.

06:58.334 --> 07:00.753
[sighs] I didn't realize
I'd have to learn so much.

07:00.837 --> 07:02.171
Come on.

07:03.005 --> 07:06.384
I keep saying,
it's not too late to change your mind.

07:06.884 --> 07:09.887
Revenge is not good, and violent as hell.

07:10.471 --> 07:14.225
I know some intense guys
who are fine with some violence.

07:14.308 --> 07:15.977
I grew up with them at the group home.

07:17.979 --> 07:20.398
You think your friends
would kill someone for me?

07:22.316 --> 07:23.234
Kill someone?

07:25.361 --> 07:27.321
I don't know exactly what I need,

07:27.822 --> 07:31.367
but I've come too far
for this to be some half-assed crime.

07:32.785 --> 07:35.121
I need to do this step by step, carefully.

07:36.456 --> 07:37.457
Of course.

07:38.624 --> 07:41.794
[Seong-hee sighs] But you're
at least halfway there, though.

07:43.880 --> 07:48.050
I read today that Park Yeon-jin is
getting married. Did you see?

07:49.469 --> 07:50.303
Mmm.

07:52.805 --> 07:54.474
I guess her dream came true.

07:56.642 --> 07:58.060
Of course it did.

08:01.898 --> 08:05.067
Know what's really great
about not being religious, Seong-hee?

08:09.989 --> 08:12.158
You know where you go when you die.

08:14.285 --> 08:15.286
To hell.

08:23.002 --> 08:27.340
[Dong-eun] So, if I'm going to hell,

08:28.508 --> 08:29.675
I will do this.

08:31.260 --> 08:33.304
Step by step.

08:34.764 --> 08:38.184
A BOOK ON THE GAME OF GO
THE GO STORY

08:47.777 --> 08:51.697
I hope that you still want
to see me dance, Yeon-jin.

08:54.575 --> 08:58.371
Though this time,
I think it'll be a dance with the devil.

08:59.038 --> 09:00.039
[phone chimes]

09:04.919 --> 09:07.380
CAN YOU DO AN EXTRA MATH SESSION?
YOU CAN SET THE PRICE

09:14.512 --> 09:16.514
[Dong-eun] So, the quadratic formula.

09:17.014 --> 09:19.267
We'll derive it
using the perfect square equation

09:19.350 --> 09:21.102
to solve the quadratic equation.

09:21.185 --> 09:25.022
AX squared plus BX plus C equals--

09:25.106 --> 09:26.023
Ma'am.

09:26.691 --> 09:28.776
Where did you get that shirt?

09:29.694 --> 09:30.736
Somewhere online.

09:32.655 --> 09:34.657
-Are you listening to me?
-It's pretty.

09:34.740 --> 09:37.952
You should stop ignoring me.
Your exam is coming soon.

09:38.035 --> 09:39.453
You'd look even better without it.

09:40.746 --> 09:43.833
If you let me see your boobs,
I'll do better on the exam.

09:43.916 --> 09:47.753
I mean, you'll get paid extra
if I get better scores, won't you?

09:48.671 --> 09:50.423
[Dong-eun] This doesn't
surprise me anymore.

09:50.923 --> 09:52.133
Thanks to you, Yeon-jin.

09:53.009 --> 09:56.846
I wonder how you people
always recognize the broken ones.

09:58.472 --> 10:00.891
-This will be your last session with me.
-Why?

10:00.975 --> 10:03.394
I can make money through other jobs too.

10:04.312 --> 10:06.772
You're an asshole
who'll end up in the same place,

10:07.273 --> 10:09.191
no matter what grades you end up with.

10:10.109 --> 10:11.110
Jail.

10:11.193 --> 10:13.404
You crazy, bitch?
You'll be fucked when my mom finds out.

10:14.363 --> 10:15.364
She already knows.

10:15.990 --> 10:19.076
You mom's been listening
to our lessons since the very beginning.

10:19.160 --> 10:20.995
You know that this is
being recorded, right?

10:21.078 --> 10:21.912
PARK SEUNG-HUN'S MOM

10:21.996 --> 10:24.123
Pay me more if you want me
to keep my mouth shut.

10:24.206 --> 10:25.207
[boy scoffs]

10:26.042 --> 10:27.668
God, this is fucking ridiculous.

10:28.252 --> 10:30.963
Don't you want to be a teacher?
And you do shit like this?

10:31.047 --> 10:33.633
I guess, yeah. I do now.

10:34.216 --> 10:35.217
Good luck on the test.

10:36.886 --> 10:38.054
[boy scoffs]

10:59.200 --> 11:01.369
[siren wailing in distance]

11:03.204 --> 11:05.206
[medical device beeping]

11:11.253 --> 11:14.674
[nurse] He got into a fight nearby,
so he was brought to the hospital quickly.

11:15.257 --> 11:17.426
[doctor] Seriously, you can't
give this guy a day off.

11:17.510 --> 11:19.637
[nurse] After the results
of the hearing came out,

11:19.720 --> 11:22.431
seems like that psychopath is
always on TV nowadays.

11:22.515 --> 11:23.516
[doctor] Really?

11:25.935 --> 11:27.895
[doctor] Wish we could just unplug the TV.

11:29.355 --> 11:32.108
Please give him a 10% DW
mixed with vitamin B and C.

11:32.191 --> 11:33.025
[nurse] Mmm.

11:34.568 --> 11:37.238
-Oh, the deputy director--
-I know.

11:42.451 --> 11:45.871
[woman over PA] The guardian
of patient Kim Min-Su in ward 62,

11:45.955 --> 11:47.623
please come back to the ward.

11:48.124 --> 11:53.045
The guardian of patient Kim Min-Su
in ward 62, please come back to the ward.

11:53.921 --> 11:55.923
["Wedding March" by Mendelssohn playing]

12:02.596 --> 12:04.765
-[confetti launcher pops]
-[guests cheering]

12:34.837 --> 12:37.298
[Dong-eun] Congratulations
on your wedding, Yeon-jin.

12:37.381 --> 12:40.843
I'm sorry, but I didn't bring
any congratulatory money.

12:41.886 --> 12:42.887
Oh, well.

12:42.970 --> 12:47.141
A wedding won't be
the most important event in your life.

12:50.186 --> 12:53.105
[Yeon-jin] Fog and clouds
both consist of water vapor,

12:53.189 --> 12:56.859
but what they're called changes
depending on where they were formed.

12:56.942 --> 13:00.029
If it's closer to the sky in relation
to the ground, it's called a cloud.

13:00.112 --> 13:03.324
And it's called fog
if the vapor forms closer to the ground.

13:09.205 --> 13:11.707
Is something wrong? Is there a typo?

13:12.541 --> 13:13.375
There's not.

13:14.543 --> 13:16.545
It's so well-written, I reread it.

13:17.880 --> 13:19.131
By the way,

13:19.965 --> 13:22.218
why do all of you guys scare so easily?

13:22.301 --> 13:23.385
[grunts dismissively]

13:27.306 --> 13:28.307
Seul-gi.

13:28.974 --> 13:32.436
You know all the other forecasters
talk behind my back, right?

13:33.312 --> 13:36.106
They think I'm less than them
because I can't write my own scripts.

13:36.190 --> 13:37.358
Huh?

13:37.441 --> 13:39.068
You know what I'm talking about.

13:39.151 --> 13:40.069
I'm not stupid.

13:42.112 --> 13:43.781
This is why I don't write my own.

13:44.448 --> 13:46.909
When I pay you,
I can get a script like this.

13:47.409 --> 13:49.286
But the ones I write sound like shit.

13:51.163 --> 13:51.997
Got a passport?

13:53.582 --> 13:55.292
-I don't.
-Then get one.

13:55.876 --> 13:58.295
And then tell me
a country you want to travel to.

13:58.379 --> 13:59.713
I like the script.

14:00.297 --> 14:02.758
[shaky sigh] You mean it?

14:05.469 --> 14:06.637
Thank you so much.

14:08.597 --> 14:10.850
I'll start researching places.

14:17.523 --> 14:18.732
[Yeon-jin chuckles]

14:18.816 --> 14:19.984
I'm now her god,

14:21.026 --> 14:22.778
because I can throw a little money.

14:27.491 --> 14:29.702
When driving early in the morning
or late at night,

14:29.785 --> 14:31.078
when fog is most likely to form,

14:31.161 --> 14:33.038
please turn on your hazard lights

14:33.122 --> 14:35.666
and slow down
to ensure that you can drive safely.

14:35.749 --> 14:36.917
[barking]

14:45.926 --> 14:47.469
Fuck off, you little asshole!

14:47.553 --> 14:48.762
[dog whimpers]

14:49.346 --> 14:51.181
[door opens, closes]

14:52.725 --> 14:54.727
-[dog barking]
-[footsteps approaching]

14:55.686 --> 14:59.356
Ugh, this fucking dog
only shits when he's back home.

14:59.440 --> 15:00.900
Little asshole.

15:00.983 --> 15:02.484
Hey, don't insult Louis.

15:03.569 --> 15:04.737
Louis XI.

15:06.655 --> 15:08.824
It's because Louis is old. He's 11 now.

15:10.159 --> 15:12.369
You're young,
so what the fuck is wrong with you?

15:13.787 --> 15:15.122
With me? What?

15:15.205 --> 15:16.206
You taking some?

15:17.583 --> 15:18.584
Some what?

15:24.131 --> 15:25.132
[man sighs]

15:26.383 --> 15:27.384
Hey.

15:29.595 --> 15:33.849
Sa-ra told me
that you keep stealing her weed.

15:35.768 --> 15:36.769
[scoffs]

15:37.478 --> 15:38.729
I wasn't stealing it. No.

15:39.563 --> 15:41.982
I was worried about Sa-ra,
and taking a little sample to--

15:42.066 --> 15:42.900
Hey.

15:44.026 --> 15:45.611
Hey. Hey!

15:49.782 --> 15:51.367
Think you can just fuck around?

15:52.326 --> 15:54.787
Or that we're still "friends"
because we hang out?

15:59.291 --> 16:01.794
I have a lot of stuff
to inherit, Myeong-o.

16:02.419 --> 16:06.840
But if I die an untimely death
because you were driving while high,

16:06.924 --> 16:08.884
that wouldn't be fair for me, would it?

16:08.968 --> 16:10.469
Hey. Answer me.

16:11.887 --> 16:13.097
Answer me, asshole!

16:17.434 --> 16:19.436
[indistinct chatter]

16:43.752 --> 16:46.046
[man] Oh! Uh, I'm sorry.

16:48.841 --> 16:51.093
[wistful, tender music playing]

16:57.057 --> 16:58.517
[medical device beeps]

17:34.470 --> 17:36.889
[beeping intensifies]

17:36.972 --> 17:38.974
[music trails off]

17:41.435 --> 17:42.936
Uh, uh, wait a second.

17:43.020 --> 17:44.104
Hey, just hold on.

17:46.148 --> 17:46.982
I, uh…

17:47.733 --> 17:49.985
I know it doesn't look like it now,

17:50.903 --> 17:53.655
but I'm an intern here, so…

17:54.740 --> 17:55.741
It's my day off.

17:56.366 --> 17:57.242
Just wait, and…

18:08.504 --> 18:10.255
Press on this for about five minutes.

18:28.774 --> 18:30.234
Wait, where'd the patient go?

18:30.943 --> 18:32.194
Mmm, she just left.

18:33.487 --> 18:35.114
Hey, I'm okay now. Hmm?

18:35.197 --> 18:36.031
HCT: HEMATOCRIT TEST

18:36.115 --> 18:37.491
Her HCT looks awful. She just left?

18:37.574 --> 18:40.285
Hey, you know, I have
a lot of pain too, huh?

18:40.369 --> 18:41.954
I just got brought in, okay?

18:42.037 --> 18:43.205
Oh, come on. I'm gonna…

18:44.289 --> 18:45.290
Ugh.

18:45.833 --> 18:47.960
Just stay still. Go back to sleep.

18:51.588 --> 18:53.173
She didn't finish her IV.

18:53.966 --> 18:55.300
Let me see. Come on.

18:59.972 --> 19:00.973
She's anemic?

19:03.559 --> 19:05.894
[man] All right,
before we start today's class,

19:05.978 --> 19:08.814
I've been wondering for a while.

19:08.897 --> 19:11.567
You in the back.
The handsome guy right there.

19:13.277 --> 19:16.822
Who are you? I really don't think
you're a student in my class.

19:16.905 --> 19:19.116
[man] Oh, hello, Professor.

19:19.199 --> 19:21.535
I heard a rumor
that your class is exceptional,

19:21.618 --> 19:23.996
so I'm sitting in.
If you'd allow me to stay--

19:24.079 --> 19:26.665
[professor] I'm guessing
there's some other "exceptional" person

19:26.748 --> 19:27.958
who's why you're here.

19:28.709 --> 19:31.003
Oh, no way!
It's definitely you, Professor!

19:31.086 --> 19:31.920
I love you so much!

19:32.004 --> 19:34.590
Oh no, that's really too bad.

19:34.673 --> 19:37.092
-I'm married, so get out.
-[class laughing]

19:37.176 --> 19:38.010
That's right.

19:38.093 --> 19:39.928
I didn't know that you were married.

19:42.222 --> 19:43.223
I'll be going now.

19:43.849 --> 19:47.102
[professor] Who is it?
Spill it. Who's so "exceptional"?

19:47.186 --> 19:49.188
[gentle, wistful music playing]

20:02.409 --> 20:04.411
[music swells]

20:06.872 --> 20:07.873
You're here.

20:12.169 --> 20:13.921
[man] I didn't hear back.
I thought you weren't here.

20:14.004 --> 20:16.632
I just have a class
I need to get credit for.

20:16.715 --> 20:19.718
-What are you doing on campus?
-Buying lunch for the kids in my club.

20:20.427 --> 20:22.429
Have you eaten? You should come with us.

20:22.512 --> 20:23.513
[Dong-eun] Mmm.

20:46.578 --> 20:49.665
How did you find out what school I go to?

20:51.375 --> 20:52.834
A nurse found your student ID

20:52.918 --> 20:54.670
while looking for the number
of your guardian.

20:54.753 --> 20:57.172
And I saw your school's name
and I went to the lecture hall

20:58.215 --> 20:59.549
because your test results…

20:59.633 --> 21:01.593
They came back, and they weren't great,

21:01.677 --> 21:03.470
so I brought your prescription.

21:04.554 --> 21:06.556
You should be more careful
with your health.

21:08.267 --> 21:10.894
You'll need to take medication
for at least six more months.

21:12.729 --> 21:15.732
The prescription I brought over
is no longer valid now.

21:16.358 --> 21:18.193
Make sure to take your meds.

21:23.156 --> 21:23.991
You like to play Go?

21:26.201 --> 21:27.452
Do you know how to play?

21:27.536 --> 21:29.663
Oh, I'm incredible.

21:32.791 --> 21:36.545
How long would I have to study Go
to beat somebody who's really good?

21:37.629 --> 21:40.465
Well, who are you trying to defeat?
Lee Se-dol?

21:41.675 --> 21:43.176
Lee Se-dol? Who is that?

21:48.557 --> 21:50.434
I think maybe you might need a tutor.

21:51.476 --> 21:53.979
Want me… as your tutor?

21:54.062 --> 21:56.064
[gentle music continuing]

21:59.651 --> 22:02.612
I have to tutor someone,
so are evenings okay for you?

22:03.113 --> 22:04.906
GYODAE CAFE

22:06.950 --> 22:08.118
Really? In 2006?

22:08.201 --> 22:09.453
[chuckles]

22:09.536 --> 22:12.456
I know, right? But yeah, I was a freshman.

22:12.956 --> 22:14.291
Oh god, I just…

22:14.833 --> 22:17.336
I feel like I'm bragging
when I talk about this,

22:17.419 --> 22:19.338
but I was born in early 1989.

22:20.213 --> 22:21.965
But I was kind of a prodigy
when I was young,

22:22.049 --> 22:23.342
so I skipped some grades.

22:24.760 --> 22:27.846
So, should I speak more formally
with a prodigy?

22:28.889 --> 22:30.474
Do you like to be formal, then?

22:32.809 --> 22:34.895
I get the black because I'm new?

22:38.815 --> 22:40.192
[man] So you already know.

22:42.069 --> 22:43.070
Put a stone on.

22:52.662 --> 22:54.790
Uh, wow.

22:57.501 --> 22:58.335
So.

23:02.130 --> 23:04.091
To sum up a game of Go,

23:04.174 --> 23:06.551
the person who has more houses
can win the game.

23:07.135 --> 23:10.013
Start near the end
and then build towards the center

23:10.097 --> 23:13.225
while building your own houses
and destroying your opponent's,

23:13.308 --> 23:16.436
and then you have to
slowly tighten your boundary.

23:17.437 --> 23:20.315
-An intense battle… in silence.
-[piece clacks]

23:26.822 --> 23:27.948
I like that.

23:30.992 --> 23:33.578
[lively, spirited music playing]

24:20.834 --> 24:22.502
I didn't study herbal medicine,

24:22.586 --> 24:24.838
but cheongsimhwan will reduce anxiety.

24:25.464 --> 24:28.508
The National Teacher Qualification Exam.
I'm sure you'll pass it.

24:32.429 --> 24:34.431
[lively, spirited music continuing]

24:43.231 --> 24:46.067
Thank you so much for helping me.

24:46.818 --> 24:48.528
You're going to be a great doctor.

24:50.030 --> 24:51.364
Am I not seeing you again?

24:52.908 --> 24:53.909
Wait, why?

24:54.451 --> 24:56.953
I need to keep tutoring you.
You haven't beaten me yet.

24:57.913 --> 25:02.000
You're not the person
I'm actually trying to beat.

25:05.462 --> 25:08.590
[man] In order to become a teacher,
you need to love humanity.

25:09.174 --> 25:10.634
This is the essence of your calling.

25:11.510 --> 25:13.803
It is your mission to provide…

25:13.887 --> 25:14.721
MOON DONG-EUN

25:14.804 --> 25:15.972
…high-quality education

25:16.056 --> 25:18.350
in order to cultivate talented students.

25:18.433 --> 25:21.311
[Dong-eun] I really liked
the spring of 2015.

25:22.020 --> 25:25.190
I passed the Teacher Qualification Exam
after my second try.

25:25.690 --> 25:28.693
And thankfully, you became a mother.

25:28.777 --> 25:30.779
[lively, spirited music trails off]

25:54.844 --> 25:55.845
[sighs]

26:01.226 --> 26:03.353
I came up with over 100 names

26:03.436 --> 26:06.648
for the child
that you'd give birth to in the fall.

26:07.649 --> 26:09.484
I even gave a little toast

26:11.570 --> 26:14.864
to my eventual moral decay,

26:16.575 --> 26:18.285
and to your destruction.

26:20.495 --> 26:22.581
SEMYEONG STREET

26:23.540 --> 26:26.543
SUMMER OF 2021

26:34.175 --> 26:35.176
[gasps]

26:36.761 --> 26:38.430
[delighted laugh]

26:42.225 --> 26:43.143
[gasps]

26:44.894 --> 26:45.895
[titters]

26:48.690 --> 26:50.483
[laughs]

26:55.822 --> 26:56.740
Happy birthday.

26:56.823 --> 26:58.450
Oh gosh, they're beautiful.

26:59.242 --> 27:01.494
Where'd you find these
in this gorgeous color?

27:03.330 --> 27:05.165
I thought you'd be able to pull it off.

27:05.248 --> 27:07.042
-[laughs]
-[phone ringing]

27:09.210 --> 27:10.211
[man] Gyeong-tae.

27:11.129 --> 27:13.548
He wants me to get a drink
with him and Sang-hyeon.

27:14.049 --> 27:16.885
-At this time of night? Crazy bastards.
-Just them?

27:17.969 --> 27:18.970
Definitely not.

27:20.096 --> 27:21.431
Sure you don't want to go?

27:21.514 --> 27:24.392
I'm sure.
The girls they're meeting are ugly.

27:24.976 --> 27:26.895
You would have gone if they were cute?

27:27.395 --> 27:28.772
How cute are we talking?

27:29.814 --> 27:30.815
[scoffs]

27:31.483 --> 27:33.652
You're just gonna brush your teeth, hmm?

27:33.735 --> 27:34.861
While I do this?

27:36.571 --> 27:38.114
That's why I'm doing it quickly.

27:38.198 --> 27:39.532
[chuckles]

27:40.492 --> 27:41.868
Gyeong-tae is so boring,

27:42.369 --> 27:44.496
and he's a complete mama's boy, too.

27:44.579 --> 27:48.333
His only attractive feature's his job,
but he's with a new girl every night.

27:48.416 --> 27:50.168
I didn't use to get that at all.

27:51.086 --> 27:52.128
And then,

27:52.629 --> 27:54.673
Hye-jeong made me realize the reason.

27:56.925 --> 27:57.926
What's the reason?

27:58.968 --> 28:01.763
I heard they did it
in the hotel lobby bathroom.

28:02.263 --> 28:04.391
They got turned on getting the hotel keys.

28:06.267 --> 28:07.227
[man spits]

28:07.727 --> 28:08.937
Crazy bastard.

28:09.020 --> 28:10.063
[chuckles]

28:10.980 --> 28:13.566
Why? I'm a little curious.

28:15.443 --> 28:18.988
The space is tiny,
and people might be nearby.

28:19.698 --> 28:21.533
The marble feels so cold,

28:22.409 --> 28:24.077
but you and I are so hot.

28:25.870 --> 28:27.497
This place is kind of like that…

28:31.793 --> 28:32.794
but it's huge.

29:02.574 --> 29:04.409
SEMYEONG
GARBAGE BAG

29:10.081 --> 29:13.126
BUILDING NUMBER
BUILDING DETAILS

29:13.209 --> 29:15.670
LAST WILL AND TESTAMENT
TESTATOR: KIM SHIN-TAE

29:21.342 --> 29:23.344
[subdued, mysterious music playing]

29:27.223 --> 29:28.600
TO MY OLD FRIEND JO SOO-HYEON

29:28.683 --> 29:29.893
I BEQUEATH THE FOLLOWING…

29:37.984 --> 29:39.027
70 SEMYEONG STREET, SEMYEONG

29:39.110 --> 29:40.236
DONATED OVER 30 BILLION WON IN 10 YEARS

29:40.320 --> 29:41.488
SEMYEONG FOUNDATION

29:41.571 --> 29:43.656
KIM SHIN-TAE'S FAMILY TREE

29:45.950 --> 29:49.162
Cho Su-hyeon isn't
in Kim Sin-tae's direct line of descent.

29:54.042 --> 29:57.420
TO MY OLD FRIEND JO SOO-HYEON…

30:05.970 --> 30:07.222
CIALIS

30:07.305 --> 30:08.807
[footsteps approaching]

30:10.642 --> 30:11.935
[Yeon-jin laughs]

30:12.018 --> 30:13.645
After a couple months here,

30:13.728 --> 30:16.856
this garden's still one of
my favorite things about this house.

30:17.732 --> 30:19.943
It looks expensive when the sun's up,

30:20.443 --> 30:22.737
and even expensive as the sun goes down.

30:22.821 --> 30:25.532
-[both laugh]
-Guess it's worth my money, then.

30:27.242 --> 30:29.744
Is the commute okay?
It's a two-hour round trip to Seoul.

30:30.245 --> 30:31.913
I like it. It keeps me fit.

30:31.996 --> 30:35.500
You said you don't like women who let
themselves get fat after marriage, right?

30:36.000 --> 30:39.128
I'll wake up at 2:00 a.m.
and jump rope on an empty stomach.

30:39.212 --> 30:41.422
If I leave at 3:00, I'll be right on time.

30:41.506 --> 30:42.549
[Yeon-jin giggles]

30:42.632 --> 30:44.092
Why so early? It's a different show?

30:44.676 --> 30:46.594
It's because I'm old now, you know?

30:47.929 --> 30:48.763
[giggles]

30:48.847 --> 30:50.723
Speaking of which, babe,

30:50.807 --> 30:54.978
is there any way you can give
our news network some ads?

30:55.061 --> 30:57.647
[laughs] I need something
to leverage when I renew my contract.

30:58.231 --> 30:59.858
You should have told me earlier.

31:00.859 --> 31:02.110
If money could fix it…

31:02.193 --> 31:03.570
[gasps]

31:03.653 --> 31:06.781
…then I think it's just about
the easiest problem in the world.

31:06.865 --> 31:08.199
[squeals] Really?

31:08.867 --> 31:10.451
You're so awesome.

31:13.788 --> 31:16.958
So, will the PR team come to the station?

31:18.251 --> 31:19.085
They will.

31:21.254 --> 31:22.422
Those new cigarettes?

31:23.047 --> 31:23.882
Huh?

31:24.674 --> 31:25.592
Uh-huh.

31:30.054 --> 31:33.099
That friend of yours,
the flight attendant one?

31:33.182 --> 31:36.519
Hey, come on, her name is Hye-jeong.
You should know that by now.

31:39.480 --> 31:40.565
What about her?

31:41.065 --> 31:42.984
She told Gyeong-tae
what you were like in school.

31:43.776 --> 31:45.028
While they were drinking.

31:46.905 --> 31:49.574
What'd she say? About me?

31:52.869 --> 31:54.537
She said she had better grades than you.

31:58.082 --> 32:00.043
[laughing uproariously]

32:00.126 --> 32:02.211
That was only one time!

32:02.295 --> 32:05.048
So, are you angry
because you heard I had bad grades?

32:05.131 --> 32:07.425
I don't like
that they dragged us through the mud.

32:09.052 --> 32:10.345
It was not "us."

32:10.929 --> 32:12.597
They always gossip about me.

32:13.431 --> 32:14.599
I'll take care of it.

32:19.854 --> 32:20.772
[door opens]

32:20.855 --> 32:21.856
[child] Mommy!

32:21.940 --> 32:22.941
[Yeon-jin] Oh!

32:25.652 --> 32:27.820
Hi, Ye-sol.

32:28.780 --> 32:30.490
What do we do first when we get back?

32:30.573 --> 32:33.576
Wash my hands. I need to wash my hands!

32:37.538 --> 32:39.624
[sighs heavily] Oh my God.

32:39.707 --> 32:41.542
Now, that totally terrified me.

32:41.626 --> 32:43.795
You too. What do you do first
after smoking?

32:44.295 --> 32:46.339
You're so cute. [Yeon-jin laughs]

32:49.467 --> 32:50.885
[phone chimes]

32:50.969 --> 32:52.553
Oh, shit…

32:52.637 --> 32:53.471
ARTIST LEE

32:53.554 --> 32:55.139
[Lee] Where are you?

32:55.223 --> 32:56.891
Why is she so annoying today?

33:04.482 --> 33:05.483
Hmm.

33:06.234 --> 33:07.151
[chuckles]

33:08.236 --> 33:09.237
Hmm.

33:09.862 --> 33:10.863
It's pretty.

33:12.907 --> 33:13.908
[both laughing]

33:15.618 --> 33:16.786
[footsteps approaching]

33:20.665 --> 33:22.250
What? What's up?

33:24.085 --> 33:25.670
[woman 1] That a new dress?

33:25.753 --> 33:27.672
Oh. Yeah, it is.

33:27.755 --> 33:29.757
My boyfriend bought it for me
at the Galleria.

33:29.841 --> 33:31.259
[laughing]

33:31.926 --> 33:32.885
Hye-jeong.

33:34.345 --> 33:35.680
Is Sa-ra your boyfriend?

33:38.433 --> 33:40.518
Have you always "borrowed"
your customers' clothes?

33:40.601 --> 33:41.978
I told you she would,

33:42.478 --> 33:44.981
that she'd show up wearing your dress
if you gave it to her.

33:45.481 --> 33:47.150
At least she has good taste.

33:47.650 --> 33:50.236
if she picked your dress
out of all those clothes.

33:50.319 --> 33:51.738
Hey, Hye-jeong.

33:52.697 --> 33:54.866
I lost a Chanel today thanks to you.

33:54.949 --> 33:57.410
God, just use perfume.
Aren't you rich, huh?

33:57.493 --> 33:59.871
The product quality
matters more than the price.

33:59.954 --> 34:01.664
This gets rid of smells best.

34:05.001 --> 34:06.002
Ugh.

34:06.753 --> 34:08.921
There are only
two of these in the country.

34:09.964 --> 34:13.176
So, I guess now
you've got high standards, huh?

34:17.555 --> 34:18.389
Hye-jeong.

34:19.807 --> 34:20.808
Know your place.

34:22.477 --> 34:24.437
If it hadn't been Dong-eun back then…

34:26.481 --> 34:28.441
it would have ended up being you.

34:28.524 --> 34:29.525
Got that?

34:30.693 --> 34:31.778
[Yeon-jin] Hye-jeong.

34:33.946 --> 34:36.824
Gyeong-tae is terrible at keeping secrets.

34:38.951 --> 34:40.495
And you gossiped about me?

34:43.372 --> 34:45.833
You should have stuck
to drinking and fucking him.

34:46.959 --> 34:49.629
Why'd you start talking about
shit from the past?

34:50.963 --> 34:51.964
Huh?

34:53.466 --> 34:55.134
We're not in high school anymore.

34:55.635 --> 34:57.970
You think we'll stay friends
no matter what?

34:59.764 --> 35:01.599
From now on, watch your mouth.

35:03.017 --> 35:04.685
And wear clothes you can afford.

35:04.769 --> 35:06.437
Know your place, Hye-jeong.

35:07.939 --> 35:09.524
Nod if you understand.

35:09.607 --> 35:11.609
[tense music playing]

35:21.536 --> 35:22.662
I'm taking this, okay?

35:26.749 --> 35:27.875
[Hye-jeong shudders]

35:28.876 --> 35:32.296
Sa-ra, I'm so sorry about this.
I'll get this dress cleaned and I--

35:32.380 --> 35:34.757
Hey, you crazy bitch.

35:36.008 --> 35:37.260
You stretched it out.

35:38.094 --> 35:39.011
You can keep it.

35:55.444 --> 35:56.571
[shutter snapping]

36:02.869 --> 36:05.454
[Hye-jeong] A gift from my friends.
Thank you, guys!

36:05.538 --> 36:08.624
Surprise! With the lovely Park Yeon-jin.

36:08.708 --> 36:10.418
[anchor] The weather is changing rapidly

36:10.501 --> 36:12.545
as we're approaching
the first weekend of March.

36:12.628 --> 36:14.130
What can you tell us, Ms. Park?

36:15.047 --> 36:17.967
I am now standing in front of
the Gilsangsa Temple in Seoul.

36:18.050 --> 36:21.637
As you can see, the spring flowers have
bloomed beautifully around the temple.

36:21.721 --> 36:24.390
Particularly interesting is
the winter jasmine,

36:24.473 --> 36:25.683
which means "welcoming spring."

36:26.517 --> 36:27.852
During the Joseon Dynasty,

36:27.935 --> 36:29.812
these flowers were
gives to the best in exams,

36:29.896 --> 36:32.023
which is why they're
known as the King's flowers.

36:32.106 --> 36:34.650
However, with the spring rain
that started yesterday,

36:34.734 --> 36:36.777
temperatures are dropping
all over the country.

36:36.861 --> 36:39.322
The rain is expected
to continue over the weekend,

36:39.405 --> 36:41.657
and will lead to a few very cold days.

36:42.158 --> 36:44.744
The temperatures are
seven degrees lower than average.

36:44.827 --> 36:47.413
In the mountainous regions,
the rain has already turned to snow,

36:47.496 --> 36:49.957
which might be continuing
today and tomorrow.

36:50.791 --> 36:52.835
If you're planning on
taking a weekend hike…

36:52.919 --> 36:55.254
I watch the weather channel every day.

36:55.922 --> 36:59.508
…in temperature between morning and night,
so please dress with care.

36:59.592 --> 37:00.718
This is Park Yeon-jin.

37:01.594 --> 37:03.596
[moody, dramatic music playing]

37:06.474 --> 37:09.060
A NEW TOMORROW WITH JAEPYEONG
A FUTURE BUILT WITH JAEPYEONG

37:09.560 --> 37:10.436
JAEPYEONG CONSTRUCTION

37:34.835 --> 37:37.046
Ugh, not him again. Seriously?

37:37.129 --> 37:39.966
I told you
that you shouldn't go outside, no?

37:40.049 --> 37:42.635
[man] I was bored,
and wanted to get some fresh air.

37:43.803 --> 37:45.554
What are you doing out in the rain?

37:46.305 --> 37:47.682
Did you get stood up again?

37:47.765 --> 37:49.058
What? Who, me?

37:50.017 --> 37:52.937
Not at all. I've never gotten stood up.

37:53.020 --> 37:55.106
I know you're dying inside.

37:55.690 --> 37:57.483
I wonder if the director knows about this.

37:57.566 --> 37:58.776
Ugh, come on.

37:59.318 --> 38:01.404
Don't get my family involved in all this.

38:01.487 --> 38:04.824
[man] I'll think about it if you let me
have a sip of that coffee you're holding.

38:04.907 --> 38:06.492
[Dr. Joo] That's not happening.

38:06.575 --> 38:08.286
Hey! Why are you stepping
in all the puddles?

38:08.369 --> 38:09.370
-Huh?
-Come over here.

38:09.453 --> 38:10.913
-Okay, okay.
-Seriously.

38:13.541 --> 38:14.542
[man chuckles]

38:16.794 --> 38:18.254
[bells jingle]

38:18.879 --> 38:20.965
God, it's raining like crazy out there.

38:23.884 --> 38:25.136
Jae-jun called, right?

38:25.219 --> 38:27.388
Uh, yeah, he needs more sweaters from you.

38:29.640 --> 38:30.641
Hold on.

38:34.061 --> 38:35.062
Oh, shit…

38:35.146 --> 38:37.231
[brooding pop song playing over speakers]

38:57.001 --> 38:57.918
Huh?

38:59.003 --> 38:59.879
Is that Dong-eun?

39:04.800 --> 39:05.718
It is.

39:07.011 --> 39:09.347
Whoa, what a coincidence.

39:10.264 --> 39:12.516
It's Myeong-o. You remember?

39:13.392 --> 39:14.393
Of course.

39:15.102 --> 39:16.479
It's been such a long time.

39:16.562 --> 39:17.646
Right.

39:19.523 --> 39:20.566
Wow…

39:22.651 --> 39:24.987
How've you been? What do you do?

39:26.030 --> 39:27.073
I'm a teacher now.

39:27.156 --> 39:29.200
Oh, really?

39:29.283 --> 39:30.910
I've been thinking about you a lot.

39:32.661 --> 39:33.662
You have?

39:37.792 --> 39:38.793
You buying those?

39:39.752 --> 39:42.129
Oh, no, I was just trying them on.

39:45.508 --> 39:47.176
No, no, no. Keep them on.

39:47.760 --> 39:48.761
They look nice.

39:50.888 --> 39:51.889
Here.

39:51.972 --> 39:53.974
[dark, intense music playing]

39:59.146 --> 40:00.147
Go look at them.

40:17.498 --> 40:20.209
Want a drink with me? Whatever you want.

40:21.419 --> 40:22.545
You can keep those on.

40:23.421 --> 40:24.880
The store's basically mine.

40:31.846 --> 40:34.265
Water, coffee, or booze?

40:37.643 --> 40:39.645
[dark, intense music continuing]

40:40.938 --> 40:41.939
Coffee.

40:44.692 --> 40:45.693
[door opens]

40:47.820 --> 40:49.530
-[door closes]
-[coffeemaker whirs]

40:58.122 --> 41:00.499
So, what were you thinking about me?

41:05.546 --> 41:06.547
Was I…

41:07.798 --> 41:08.966
Was I your first kiss?

41:10.217 --> 41:12.720
Heh. Makes sense I was on your mind.

41:15.222 --> 41:18.058
Tell me now, is this store really yours?

41:19.101 --> 41:20.019
More or less.

41:21.020 --> 41:22.229
I dabble here and there.

41:23.230 --> 41:24.773
So I'm pretty busy, you know?

41:25.941 --> 41:27.735
[clerk] Hey, Jae-jun called.

41:27.818 --> 41:29.737
He wants to know
why you're not picking up.

41:29.820 --> 41:32.448
He wants you to grab
his clothes from the laundromat

41:32.531 --> 41:33.949
and buy some dog food, too.

41:37.578 --> 41:38.579
[Myeong-o chuckles]

41:38.662 --> 41:40.456
God, he's such an asshole. Shit.

41:42.124 --> 41:44.043
That guy can't do anything without me.

41:44.919 --> 41:47.004
That's Jae-jun, remember?

41:48.589 --> 41:49.965
I guess nothing's changed.

41:50.466 --> 41:52.718
Because you are
still his little errand boy.

41:52.801 --> 41:54.303
Hey, come on, cut it out.

41:54.386 --> 41:56.222
Life is so unfair.

41:57.598 --> 42:01.101
While I was training to be a teacher
and you were getting him dog food,

42:01.185 --> 42:04.063
he inherited a golf course
and now owns this store,

42:04.146 --> 42:05.564
because he was born lucky.

42:07.358 --> 42:10.986
That's why I hoped
all this belonged to you.

42:11.070 --> 42:12.863
For a second I really hoped it did.

42:13.447 --> 42:14.615
Are you trying to insult me?

42:17.576 --> 42:18.536
Watch your mouth.

42:19.537 --> 42:20.663
I can still hit you.

42:24.458 --> 42:26.460
How about you pick another punching bag?

42:27.753 --> 42:30.589
If you do that,
maybe everything here could be yours.

42:31.173 --> 42:32.424
The hell do you mean?

42:32.508 --> 42:34.843
I learned something
pretty intense recently.

42:35.636 --> 42:38.556
I don't think
that I can handle it by myself.

42:38.639 --> 42:40.641
[mysterious music playing]

42:44.645 --> 42:47.189
Do you want to know
why I'm telling you all this?

42:47.690 --> 42:50.359
I thought you'd understand
wanting to destroy them.

42:51.986 --> 42:52.820
And also,

42:54.154 --> 42:55.864
back when everything happened,

42:56.865 --> 42:58.534
I was actually scared of you

42:59.326 --> 43:00.411
more than the others.

43:05.416 --> 43:06.292
You were?

43:08.669 --> 43:09.587
What is it?

43:10.754 --> 43:12.339
This "intense" stuff?

43:12.423 --> 43:13.549
[bar patrons chatter]

43:16.343 --> 43:19.138
So you don't drink much,
but you can hold your liquor.

43:20.014 --> 43:23.934
I'm usually drunk after one glass,
but I guess I'm just excited today.

43:24.018 --> 43:27.187
Uh, that's good to hear.
Makes me feel special.

43:27.771 --> 43:30.065
Aw, no, come on.
Of course you're special to me.

43:31.358 --> 43:32.359
Huh?

43:32.443 --> 43:33.861
By the way, I want to ask…

43:34.820 --> 43:37.072
So do you wear that watch all the time?

43:37.156 --> 43:38.240
Watch?

43:39.533 --> 43:43.120
Uh… My dad bought this
when he was assigned his first school.

43:43.203 --> 43:44.830
He wanted to pass it on to his son.

43:44.913 --> 43:47.291
He just had a thing
for creating traditions like this.

43:48.000 --> 43:50.419
Wow, so sweet.

43:51.295 --> 43:52.254
But he's old.

43:53.255 --> 43:57.217
It's hard to pay for his nursing staff
right now, and those hospital bills.

43:58.135 --> 44:00.554
So I really need to pass
my School Inspector Exam this time.

44:00.638 --> 44:02.222
My wife even prays for it in church.

44:03.057 --> 44:04.058
Does it work?

44:05.351 --> 44:08.187
I feel like I'm just trudging
forward on my own.

44:08.687 --> 44:10.689
I don't think God has
ever really helped me.

44:11.273 --> 44:12.107
Huh?

44:13.567 --> 44:15.361
Uh, you praying for something?

44:16.820 --> 44:20.824
Yeah. Just for you
to pass your exam this time around.

44:21.700 --> 44:23.452
I really hope that you pass.

44:23.535 --> 44:25.829
I'm rooting for you with all my heart.

44:27.081 --> 44:28.123
SEMYEONG REAL ESTATE

44:28.207 --> 44:29.041
Oh, thanks.

44:29.541 --> 44:32.753
You know, when you're drinking,
your eyes look so pretty.

44:32.836 --> 44:33.837
Is that so?

44:35.381 --> 44:36.965
Well, my legs are prettier.

44:38.175 --> 44:39.968
[phone continues ringing]

44:42.429 --> 44:43.263
Mm-hmm.

44:45.224 --> 44:46.225
Yes, hello?

44:46.767 --> 44:49.687
[woman] Hello, I'm calling
from Semyeong Real Estate.

44:53.399 --> 44:56.777
There's a vacancy in the apartment
that you were interested in renting.

44:56.860 --> 44:57.695
RENTAL CONTRACT

44:57.778 --> 44:59.154
Bring your seal with you, okay?

45:07.579 --> 45:09.581
[intricately dramatic music building]

45:23.470 --> 45:24.471
[door opens]

45:26.890 --> 45:28.559
[woman] You're looking for this, right?

45:28.642 --> 45:29.643
[music trails off]

45:52.207 --> 45:53.625
How long have you done this?

45:54.168 --> 45:56.754
I only noticed you doing this last fall.

45:57.671 --> 45:58.839
Don't try to lie to me.

45:59.882 --> 46:02.009
You may have avoided security cameras,

46:02.634 --> 46:05.596
but I have your photos stored in my phone.

46:06.346 --> 46:09.516
I've collected pictures of you.

46:10.768 --> 46:14.021
[Dong-eun] Look at that.
God never helps me.

46:14.605 --> 46:17.357
Why did this employee
at the chairman's house

46:17.441 --> 46:19.735
have to be this observant
and this patient?

46:26.241 --> 46:28.911
If you want money from me, it's yours.

46:29.620 --> 46:32.289
I don't want money.
I'm not going to report you.

46:34.875 --> 46:36.627
I don't know what you're trying to do,

46:37.711 --> 46:39.588
but I feel like you'll succeed,

46:39.671 --> 46:41.882
since you've been doing this
for half a year.

46:43.175 --> 46:45.302
[exhales deeply]
I want to be on your side.

46:45.803 --> 46:47.638
[music intensifies]

46:47.721 --> 46:49.223
I'll help you out with what you need,

46:50.224 --> 46:51.475
so please help me, too.

46:56.021 --> 46:59.274
And what do you want me to do?

46:59.358 --> 47:01.360
[music swells, fades away]

47:02.402 --> 47:03.403
My husband…

47:05.697 --> 47:06.740
kill him.

47:19.169 --> 47:21.171
[dark, brooding pop song playing]
